# Round 18, C1-27 (follows). L §2.2 Built-in names: "any id, key, record field, bound variable or rule label may take
# one, except unit, which is also a keyword and so may name only a rule label". A bound variable named unit is
# refused (LOAD-RESERVED). (L2_2_unit_rule_label: a rule labelled unit loads.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
index ks = [a, b]
input v[k in ks]: int
def t: int = sum(v[unit] for unit in ks)
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  v[*] = 1
ask q: t
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RESERVED unit is a keyword (m.tally:9)
